<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles, Margrave of Burgau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1560–1618</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Charles of Burgau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles of Burgau was the son of Archduke Ferdinand II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-welser">Philippine Welser</a>. Because of his parents' unequal marriage he could not inherit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrol">Tyrol</a>, but he received the Margraviate of Burgau in Swabia and from 1609 resided at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunzburg">Günzburg</a>. He died without legitimate heirs in 1618, and Burgau returned to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-margrave-of-burgau.jpg" alt="Charles, Margrave of Burgau" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Domenico Custos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl-von-Burgau_(nach_1606).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
